cec: a prompt for the CEC core

LG's libcecp (eim's HDMI-CEC) drives /dev/cec0 through the CEC framework's ioctls, and lgemu.ko
registers the board's adapter with that framework (lgemu cec.c). CEC_CORE has no prompt: only an
in-tree driver can select it, and none of them fits a virtual board. Showing the prompt changes
nothing else.

--- a/drivers/media/cec/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/cec/Kconfig
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 config CEC_CORE
-	tristate
+	tristate "HDMI CEC core"

 config CEC_NOTIFIER
 	bool
